Changed duplicated singleton UTC properties to return the earliest valid timestamp. In duplicate lists, siblings that fail to decode no longer block a valid value; ``InvalidCalendar`` is raised when no valid value exists. Stored duplicates still serialize, and explicit ``VALUE=TEXT`` and ``VALUE=UNKNOWN`` values decode as before. This earliest-value policy applies to all consumers of the singleton UTC accessor. Drafted with Claude Sonnet 5, reviewed by me. @SemTiOne
